# The demand-step loop reference from plan/00-foundation/01-vision-and-scope.md (D-16).
#
# The cooling loop in time: `PB` puts 8 m of DN20 pipe in four cells on the recirculation branch,
# so a change at `HE1` reaches the measured node `N2` 38 s later; `TC1` holds `N2` at 20 C through
# the three-way valve; the schedule steps the load from 30 to 45 kW at t = 60 s.
#
# Its t = 0 state is the cooling loop's design state (D-141): the control line's setpoint holds
# `N2` at 20 C in the design solve and chooses the valve position. Until P6.0 builds that rule the
# script does not solve (S-75), and until C-113 closes the pipe's stated dn is lost by its cells;
# it is committed as the reference and stays out of CorpusStatusTests until it solves.

fluidscript 1
circuit demandStep
fluid dynamic water
show temperature

HE1 heat_exchanger power=30 out.t=50
3WV three_way_valve
PU1 pump
P1  pipe length=25
PB  pipe length=8 dn=20 nodes=4   # recirculation branch — the path the controller sees
TC1 pi                            # definition: algorithm and gains (D-40)

control actuate=3WV.position measure=N2.t by=TC1 setpoint=20

connections
N1 - N2
N2 - PU1
PU1 - HE1
HE1 - 3WV
3WV - PB - N2                # recirculation, now with volume in it
3WV - P1
P1 - N3

N1 inlet t=6 p=300
N3 outlet p=280

schedule
at 60 s   HE1.power = 45
